{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795543746,"nonce":"OFtWSWaYLYK2/wAedcpaowKpzks=","target":"0d4b6369ef9d99be352031fa232ec492cccd4488023ccaab41a63f329878f73e","message":"On a CPU with four XLA threads or fewer (a 4-vCPU GitHub runner, or `taskset -c 0-3`), a steady 8 x 8 Roe gas solve with `jno.fvm` never finishes. The CI shard \"core 2/4\" timed out after 100 minutes on PR #345. A machine with more threads solves it. Versions: JAX/jaxlib 0.10.1, scipy 1.18.\n\n**Reproduce.** `tests/test_coupling_participants.py::test_a_steady_roe_gas_solves_on_a_cpu_with_two_threads` runs `_steady_gas_2d()` in a fresh process pinned to two threads (JAX sizes its CPU pool at start). Before the workaround it timed out at 400 s. With the workaround reverted, any run pinned with `taskset -c 0-3` reproduces it.\n\n**What gdb shows.** The main thread waits in `CpuPjRtRawLoadedExecutable::Execute`. All four XLA intra-op pool threads sit in `lapack_dtrsm_ffi` -\u003e `TriMatrixEquationSolver::Kernel` -\u003e `jax::ParallelBatchMap`, each waiting for batch pieces it queued on the same pool. No thread is free to run them, so the program deadlocks.\n\n**Where.** The batched kernels came from `jnp.linalg.inv` and `jnp.linalg.solve` on small per-face blocks in `jno/_fvm/trace.py`: the Roe |A| (Denman-Beavers iteration, 112x5x5 interior and 32x5x5 boundary faces), the face Newton steps (8x4x4 and 8x1x1) and the algebraic-row completion. The program also holds JAX's `spsolve` host callback (`lu()` on the CPU). A pure-JAX script with the same Denman-Beavers inverses in a `fori_loop` did not hang on 2 or 4 threads, so the trigger needs more of the program than the kernels alone. It is not reduced further.\n\n**Workaround (in #345, commit 730610f2).** `_small_solve` in `jno/_fvm/trace.py` is an unrolled Gauss-Jordan elimination with partial pivoting in jnp. It replaces the batched LAPACK calls at the three call sites above, and the test above guards it.\n\n**Direction.** The fvm call sites are covered; the root cause is not. Other jNO code that runs batched `jnp.linalg` (LU, triangular solves) inside a large CPU program on a small machine may deadlock the same way. Two steps remain: audit those paths, and check whether a newer jaxlib fixes `ParallelBatchMap` on the intra-op pool. If it does not, build a reduced reproduction and report it upstream.\n\nCited as git-bug ad3129c in the commit history.","files":null}]}